{"id": "BT-0051", "category": "recon", "issue": "Reece Plumbing Supply invoice 88412 was entered twice; BT-0051 is the copy that is not on the bank statement.", "proposed_fix": "Delete or void BT-0051 (the $1,848.00 duplicate). Keep BT-0050, which is matched to SL-0011's counterpart SL-0050. This removes $1,680.00 of Materials (310) and $168.00 of GST credit that were counted twice.", "evidence": "BT-0051: Contact Reece Plumbing Supply, Date 2026-08-12, Reference \"88412\", Materials J-121, AccountCode 310, LineAmount 1680.00, TaxAmount 168.00, Total 1848.00, IsReconciled false. BT-0050: Contact Reece Plumbing Supply, Date 2026-08-11, Reference \"INV 88412\", Materials job J-121, Total 1848.00, IsReconciled true, matched by SL-0050 (2026-08-11, REECE PLUMBING SUPPLY, -1848.00). Same contact, same total, same invoice number in a different format. No statement line matches BT-0051.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:18"}
{"id": "BT-0047", "category": "coding", "issue": "An install job billed by joinery subcontractor Pinewood Joinery was coded to Materials instead of Subcontractors, which misstates job costing for J-118.", "proposed_fix": "Recode the line from 310 Materials to 315 Subcontractors, $5,800.00 ex GST (total $6,380.00). If the invoice includes supplied materials as well as labour, ask the client for it so the lines can be split.", "evidence": "BT-0047, 2026-08-22, Contact Pinewood Joinery (DefaultAccountCode 315), Description \"Joinery install, job J-118\", AccountCode 310, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 5800.00, TaxAmount 580.00, Total 6380.00. Pinewood's other claims (BT-0030, BT-0031, BT-0033) are all coded to 315.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:20"}
{"id": "BT-0052", "category": "recon", "issue": "BT-0052 is recorded at $1,254.00, but the statement line it is matched to shows $1,524.00. That is a $270.00 difference and looks like transposed digits.", "proposed_fix": "Check Coastal Electrical Contractors' invoice for the job J-124 progress claim. If the invoice is $1,524.00, the bank amount is correct: change BT-0052 to Total 1524.00 (LineAmount 1385.45 plus GST 138.55, account 315) and re-reconcile. If the invoice really is $1,254.00, the supplier was overpaid $270.00: get a credit or refund from Coastal Electrical and record it.", "evidence": "BT-0052: Contact Coastal Electrical Contractors, Date 2026-08-24, Progress claim job J-124, AccountCode 315, LineAmount 1140.00, TaxAmount 114.00, Total 1254.00, IsReconciled true. Matched statement line SL-0051: Date 2026-08-24, Payee COASTAL ELECTRICAL CON, Amount -1524.00, MatchedTransactionID BT-0052. Difference 270.00.", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:22"}
{"id": "BT-0048", "category": "coding", "issue": "A Woolworths groceries purchase on the company account was coded to Entertainment and looks like private spending.", "proposed_fix": "Ask the client whether this had a business purpose. If not, recode the full $214.35 to 880 Owner A Drawings, BAS Excluded with no GST. The GST reviewer covers the reversal of the GST credit separately.", "evidence": "BT-0048, 2026-08-23, Contact Woolworths, Description \"Groceries\", AccountCode 420 Entertainment, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 194.86, TaxAmount 19.49, Total 214.35.", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:23"}
{"id": "BT-0042", "category": "gst", "issue": "A bank fee is coded with a GST credit, but the firm's rules treat bank fees as input taxed, so no credit can be claimed.", "proposed_fix": "Change TaxType from INPUT to EXEMPTEXPENSES (input taxed) on account 404. LineAmount becomes 64.90 and TaxAmount 0.00, which reverses a GST credit of 5.90. If the CBA merchant statement is a tax invoice that shows GST on the merchant facility fee, confirm that with the client before changing it.", "evidence": "BT-0042, 2026-08-31, Contact Commonwealth Bank, Description 'Merchant facility fee', AccountCode 404 (Bank Fees, default TaxType EXEMPTEXPENSES), TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 59.00, TaxAmount 5.90, Total 64.90. The sibling fee BT-0041 is correctly coded EXEMPTEXPENSES with TaxAmount 0.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:25"}
{"id": "SL-0052", "category": "recon", "issue": "An $8,420.00 ATO payment on the bank statement has no Xero transaction, so it is missing from the books.", "proposed_fix": "This is most likely an activity statement payment (BAS or IAS, covering GST and PAYG withholding) for a prior period. Ask the client which BAS or IAS it paid. Record it as a Spend Money transaction of $8,420.00 to the ATO, coded BAS Excluded, against the GST and PAYG Withholding liability accounts (or the ATO integrated client account clearing account), split as the lodged statement shows. To confirm, get the ATO Integrated Client Account statement and the lodged BAS or IAS showing the $8,420.00 amount owing.", "evidence": "SL-0052: Date 2026-08-28, Payee ATO PAYMENT, Amount -8420.00, MatchedTransactionID null. None of BT-0001 to BT-0052 has contact ATO or a total of 8420.00.", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:25"}
{"id": "BT-0049", "category": "coding", "issue": "A 12-month contract works insurance premium was expensed in full to Insurance in August, when it covers August 2026 to July 2027 and should go to Prepayments.", "proposed_fix": "Recode the $4,800.00 ex GST to 620 Prepayments, keeping the $480.00 GST credit on the bill. Release $400.00 a month ($4,800.00 / 12) to 433 Insurance, starting with August 2026. The August 2026 expense is $400.00, and $4,400.00 stays in Prepayments at 31 Aug 2026.", "evidence": "BT-0049, 2026-08-02, Contact QBE Insurance, Description \"Contract works insurance, 12 months to 31 Jul 2027\", AccountCode 433, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 4800.00, TaxAmount 480.00, Total 5280.00. CapitaliseThreshold 1000.0.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:26"}
{"id": "BT-0043", "category": "gst", "issue": "A GST credit was claimed on a payment to a supplier that is not registered for GST.", "proposed_fix": "Change TaxType from INPUT to GST free (no GST credit). LineAmount becomes 3,960.00 and TaxAmount 0.00, which reverses a GST credit of 360.00. Account 315 stays as it is.", "evidence": "BT-0043, 2026-08-26, Contact Ridge Tiling (sole trader) (C006, TaxNumber 71 824 330 016, IsGSTRegistered false), Description 'Tiling, job J-121', AccountCode 315, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 3600.00, TaxAmount 360.00, Total 3960.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:28"}
{"id": "BT-0044", "category": "gst", "issue": "Wages are coded with a GST credit, but wages are BAS Excluded.", "proposed_fix": "Change TaxType from INPUT to BASEXCLUDED on account 477. LineAmount becomes 3,300.00 and TaxAmount 0.00, which reverses a GST credit of 300.00.", "evidence": "BT-0044, 2026-08-17, Contact Payroll Clearing (IsGSTRegistered false), Description 'Weekly wages (casual)', AccountCode 477 (Wages and Salaries, default BASEXCLUDED), TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 3000.00, TaxAmount 300.00, Total 3300.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:30"}
{"id": "BT-0045", "category": "gst", "issue": "GST was calculated as 10% of the total instead of 1/11 of the total, so the GST credit is overstated by 19.80.", "proposed_fix": "Correct TaxAmount to 198.00 (2,178.00 / 11) and LineAmount to 1,980.00. Total stays at 2,178.00.", "evidence": "BT-0045, 2026-08-09, Contact Laminex Direct (IsGSTRegistered true), Description 'Benchtop laminate, job J-124', AccountCode 310, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 1960.20, TaxAmount 217.80, Total 2178.00. 2178.00 / 11 = 198.00; 217.80 = 10% x 2178.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:33"}
{"id": "BT-0048", "category": "gst", "issue": "A GST credit was claimed on groceries, which look like private spending with no business purpose.", "proposed_fix": "If the client confirms the spending is private, change TaxType from INPUT to BASEXCLUDED (the coding reviewer is proposing a move to 880 Owner A Drawings). LineAmount becomes 214.35 and TaxAmount 0.00, which reverses a GST credit of 19.49. Ask the client whether these groceries had any business use, such as staff amenities or client catering.", "evidence": "BT-0048, 2026-08-23, Contact Woolworths, Description 'Groceries', AccountCode 420 (Entertainment), TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 194.86, TaxAmount 19.49, Total 214.35.", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:01:36"}

